1
00:00:25,331 --> 00:00:27,131
Come on. I'm so cold.

2
00:00:27,211 --> 00:00:28,041
Ragnarok

3
00:00:28,131 --> 00:00:31,051
How long do we have to wait here?

4
00:00:31,131 --> 00:00:33,051
We're not earning anything.

5
00:00:33,131 --> 00:00:35,631
The prince got scared.

6
00:00:35,721 --> 00:00:39,641
So we were right about Wessex.

7
00:00:39,721 --> 00:00:40,811
I'm sure about it.

8
00:00:41,931 --> 00:00:44,521
We got the short end of the stick--

9
00:00:48,981 --> 00:00:55,611
Take that!

10
00:00:56,821 --> 00:00:59,581
-There's another one!
-Get away! Get away!

11
00:01:04,161 --> 00:01:05,871
Hey!

12
00:01:05,961 --> 00:01:08,041
Hurry up and attack!

13
00:01:08,131 --> 00:01:11,551
You'll never go to Valhalla at this rate!

14
00:01:11,631 --> 00:01:14,381
Are you just going to stand there?

15
00:01:14,471 --> 00:01:17,551
You're just a bunch of scarecrows!

16
00:01:17,641 --> 00:01:20,511
-Damn that bastard!
-He's so full of himself!

17
00:01:20,601 --> 00:01:25,771
None of you has any balls!

18
00:01:28,601 --> 00:01:30,021
Ragnar!

19
00:01:31,691 --> 00:01:33,651
Letting him insult us like this

20
00:01:33,731 --> 00:01:36,531
is a disgrace to us warriors! Let's attack!

21
00:01:36,611 --> 00:01:38,491
We're ready to fight!

22
00:01:38,571 --> 00:01:41,951
We have 4000 men. I'm sure we can beat Thorkell!

23
00:01:42,951 --> 00:01:46,161
Not yet. We're talking about Thorkell.

24
00:01:46,251 --> 00:01:48,171
We can't make a careless move.

25
00:01:48,251 --> 00:01:51,501
His Highness put us in charge of the siege.

26
00:01:51,591 --> 00:01:54,131
This is our chance to distinguish ourselves
as warriors!

27
00:01:54,211 --> 00:01:55,381
No.

28
00:01:55,881 --> 00:01:59,431
When the time comes,
His Highness shall give the order.

29
00:01:59,511 --> 00:02:01,351
Now is the time to wait.

30
00:02:01,431 --> 00:02:03,101
Ragnar!

31
00:02:09,141 --> 00:02:12,821
And then the Lord was told,

32
00:02:12,901 --> 00:02:15,071
"Put your sword back into its place,

33
00:02:16,111 --> 00:02:20,361
for all those who take up the sword
shall perish by the sword."

34
00:02:22,451 --> 00:02:26,701
Father. Excuse me. Can you leave us alone
for a moment?

35
00:02:31,461 --> 00:02:34,921
-Orders? Who cares!
-The prince is a coward!

36
00:02:35,001 --> 00:02:36,671
I'm not going to sit here silent!

37
00:02:36,761 --> 00:02:38,131
Yeah! Let's do it!

38
00:02:38,221 --> 00:02:39,631
Yeah! That's right!

39
00:02:40,721 --> 00:02:42,721
Don't worry.

40
00:02:42,801 --> 00:02:46,221
When winter comes,
we will receive the order to withdraw.

41
00:02:46,311 --> 00:02:48,311
We'll just have to endure until then.

42
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,191
Come on! You're kidding me!

43
00:02:55,271 --> 00:02:58,941
God, please protect His Highness.

44
00:03:00,401 --> 00:03:04,331
Damn! What's wrong with you? You guys are no fun!

45
00:03:05,411 --> 00:03:07,661
You're hard at work too.

46
00:03:07,751 --> 00:03:09,081
Are they being mean again?

47
00:03:09,161 --> 00:03:10,791
Shut up, Asgeir.

48
00:03:10,871 --> 00:03:14,881
We can't have a battle if they don't attack!

49
00:03:14,961 --> 00:03:19,261
Don't be so loud. I bet they're just being more careful.

50
00:03:19,341 --> 00:03:23,261
They're under the command of the Prince of Denmark.

51
00:03:23,341 --> 00:03:24,221
What?

52
00:03:26,391 --> 00:03:29,181
What? Is the Prince here?

53
00:03:29,271 --> 00:03:30,941
Huh? I thought I already told you.

54
00:03:31,981 --> 00:03:34,651
The second prince, His Highness Canute.

55
00:05:39,561 --> 00:05:41,271
Mother's here.

56
00:05:44,361 --> 00:05:45,651
And my sister too.

57
00:05:48,241 --> 00:05:51,991
Ari is slacking off again watching the sheep.

58
00:05:52,081 --> 00:05:56,041
Just the other day, they were saying that
one went missing.

59
00:05:59,421 --> 00:06:03,131
That's right! It's time for dinner!
I have to go tell Father!

60
00:06:07,341 --> 00:06:09,181
Father!

61
00:06:10,181 --> 00:06:12,431
Father!

62
00:06:18,191 --> 00:06:22,311
We're having meat tonight.
We're celebrating Yule.

63
00:06:22,401 --> 00:06:26,241
Oh, really? It's already the winter solstice?

64
00:06:26,321 --> 00:06:29,071
It's pretty warm, so I had forgotten about it.

65
00:06:32,281 --> 00:06:34,581
This is a nice place.

66
00:06:34,661 --> 00:06:38,831
There's enough grass for the animals.
I'm glad we moved here.

67
00:06:40,371 --> 00:06:45,631
My sister says it's inconvenient living here
because we can't get any slaves.

68
00:06:45,711 --> 00:06:48,551
We've never even had a slave, though.

69
00:06:50,431 --> 00:06:52,091
She would say that.

70
00:06:53,261 --> 00:06:55,471
I like it here.

71
00:06:55,561 --> 00:06:58,771
Mother seems to be feeling better after we moved here.

72
00:07:02,811 --> 00:07:04,401
Thorfinn.

73
00:07:04,481 --> 00:07:05,691
What?

74
00:07:05,771 --> 00:07:07,071
You're my oldest son.

75
00:07:08,241 --> 00:07:13,071
You have to protect your mother and your sister.
You understand, right?

76
00:07:13,161 --> 00:07:14,241
Yeah.

77
00:07:15,781 --> 00:07:18,701
They're both waiting for you to come home.

78
00:07:20,791 --> 00:07:23,001
Having people like that

79
00:07:23,081 --> 00:07:25,171
is a happy thing.

80
00:07:31,841 --> 00:07:32,931
Do you understand?

81
00:07:37,761 --> 00:07:41,811
So stop thinking about revenge.

82
00:07:41,891 --> 00:07:44,691
Do you think that would make me happy?

83
00:08:04,671 --> 00:08:05,671
The village!

84
00:08:06,751 --> 00:08:09,711
Father! What are we going to do? We're under attack!

85
00:08:09,801 --> 00:08:11,421
Mother! Sister!

86
00:08:34,321 --> 00:08:36,371
Father!

87
00:09:03,431 --> 00:09:06,191
Where was that?

88
00:09:07,481 --> 00:09:09,191
Somewhere warm...

89
00:09:09,271 --> 00:09:11,481
with rolling plains of grass...

90
00:09:11,571 --> 00:09:12,991
as far as the eye can see...

91
00:09:37,131 --> 00:09:40,721
NOVEMBER, 1013
OUTSKIRTS OF BATH

92
00:10:00,371 --> 00:10:05,001
What in the world is our leader thinking?

93
00:10:09,331 --> 00:10:11,171
It's almost winter.

94
00:10:11,251 --> 00:10:14,251
The main army withdrew to the north
a long time ago.

95
00:10:14,341 --> 00:10:17,841
But we're still here picking off
gloomy villages like this.

96
00:10:17,921 --> 00:10:22,601
Well, we have to earn what we can
before going back.

97
00:10:22,681 --> 00:10:26,141
Then we should attack a bigger city!

98
00:10:26,221 --> 00:10:28,311
Bristol is near here, right?

99
00:10:28,391 --> 00:10:29,981
Are you stupid?

100
00:10:30,061 --> 00:10:32,731
What can we do with only 100 men?

101
00:10:32,811 --> 00:10:34,821
What? Stupid?

102
00:10:34,901 --> 00:10:36,401
Did you just call me stupid?

103
00:10:36,491 --> 00:10:38,651
Huh, you heard me?

104
00:10:38,741 --> 00:10:41,571
I guess your ears aren't stupid.

105
00:10:41,661 --> 00:10:43,451
What did you say?

106
00:10:43,531 --> 00:10:44,831
What's wrong with you?

107
00:10:44,911 --> 00:10:46,701
What? I'm going to kill you!

108
00:10:48,501 --> 00:10:53,091
Well, all that's left for this year
is to plunder two or three more villages.

109
00:10:53,171 --> 00:10:55,461
I hope next year's going to be better.

110
00:10:57,341 --> 00:10:59,421
Do you think we'll still have a chance
next year?

111
00:10:59,511 --> 00:11:00,341
What?

112
00:11:01,221 --> 00:11:04,811
We've been plundering England
for ten years already.

113
00:11:04,891 --> 00:11:07,471
This year was especially horrible.

114
00:11:07,561 --> 00:11:10,771
I heard that the King of England
escaped overseas.

115
00:11:13,611 --> 00:11:16,441
That means
that the King of Denmark has won.

116
00:11:16,531 --> 00:11:18,071
The war is coming to an end.

117
00:11:19,571 --> 00:11:22,281
Really? I think it's still too early.

118
00:11:22,361 --> 00:11:25,831
Thorkell's in London.

119
00:11:25,911 --> 00:11:28,791
You saw how strong he is, right?

120
00:11:28,871 --> 00:11:32,711
Thorkell, huh? He is strong.

121
00:11:32,791 --> 00:11:35,791
But he's Norse, just like us.

122
00:11:35,881 --> 00:11:40,051
Once the English are about to die,
he'd ditch them in a heartbeat.

123
00:11:41,761 --> 00:11:43,221
Kill him.

124
00:11:44,431 --> 00:11:45,261
Again?

125
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:46,681
Kill him, Tore!

126
00:11:49,771 --> 00:11:51,601
Take that!

127
00:11:51,691 --> 00:11:55,691
Hey, guys! Why are they fighting?

128
00:11:55,771 --> 00:11:58,781
Ake called Tore stupid.

129
00:11:58,861 --> 00:12:00,571
Tore got mad.

130
00:12:00,651 --> 00:12:03,821
But Ake wouldn't apologize
and insulted him even more.

131
00:12:03,911 --> 00:12:04,871
What'd he say?

132
00:12:05,821 --> 00:12:07,161
Cattle thief.

133
00:12:07,241 --> 00:12:08,541
I see.

134
00:12:08,621 --> 00:12:10,001
So that's what he said.

135
00:12:12,831 --> 00:12:14,791
Then it can't be helped.

136
00:12:14,881 --> 00:12:18,751
Just make sure you tell Askeladd afterwards,
no matter who dies.

137
00:12:18,841 --> 00:12:20,011
What a pain.

138
00:12:41,821 --> 00:12:43,281
A fertile land.

139
00:12:45,201 --> 00:12:47,411
It's like the land I saw in my dream.

140
00:12:48,741 --> 00:12:51,161
It's really different from Iceland.

141
00:12:52,161 --> 00:12:56,171
I bet the snow is beginning
to pile up around now.

142
00:13:23,901 --> 00:13:26,451
You're up early, Thorfinn.

143
00:13:29,161 --> 00:13:31,241
The sun hasn't even come up yet.

144
00:13:44,301 --> 00:13:47,801
So you couldn't sleep
because they're too loud?

145
00:13:47,881 --> 00:13:51,051
Well, go easy on them.

146
00:13:51,141 --> 00:13:54,981
They were frustrated since we've been
marching a lot these days.

147
00:13:55,061 --> 00:13:57,891
You got to relax sometimes.

148
00:13:57,981 --> 00:13:59,771
Don't talk to me like we're close!

149
00:14:02,361 --> 00:14:05,821
I think you've got the wrong idea.

150
00:14:05,901 --> 00:14:08,071
I'm not your friend.

151
00:14:09,451 --> 00:14:12,951
I bet you think you have me
under your control.

152
00:14:13,031 --> 00:14:15,411
You're full of yourself now.

153
00:14:16,581 --> 00:14:18,671
But it'll stop when I slit
your throat someday,

154
00:14:18,751 --> 00:14:20,541
and you fall over and die.

155
00:14:23,711 --> 00:14:25,171
I'm so scared.

156
00:14:25,261 --> 00:14:29,261
I never imagined that little kid would glare
at me someday. You've grown a lot.

157
00:14:32,641 --> 00:14:36,981
Well, time is on your side.

158
00:14:37,061 --> 00:14:39,981
You're going to grow,
and I'm going to get old.

159
00:14:40,061 --> 00:14:43,271
Someday, I'm going to lose to you.

160
00:14:43,361 --> 00:14:45,651
It's only natural.

161
00:14:45,731 --> 00:14:47,941
Even the strongest dies someday.

162
00:14:50,531 --> 00:14:53,241
Look around you, Thorfinn.

163
00:14:53,331 --> 00:14:56,491
These stones weren't made by the people

164
00:14:56,581 --> 00:14:58,871
who live in England now, the Saxons.

165
00:14:59,871 --> 00:15:03,291
They were made by the people who lived here
before the Saxons.

166
00:15:04,591 --> 00:15:06,801
I heard they were a strong people.

167
00:15:08,341 --> 00:15:11,381
But they were destroyed
by the Saxons 500 years ago.

168
00:15:13,011 --> 00:15:14,391
They were the Romans.

169
00:15:15,431 --> 00:15:17,811
The name of their country was Britannia.

170
00:15:22,981 --> 00:15:25,071
They had an advanced civilization.

171
00:15:25,151 --> 00:15:26,731
More advanced than what we have now.

172
00:15:29,191 --> 00:15:31,281
Stop beating around the bush.

173
00:15:31,361 --> 00:15:33,161
What are you trying to say?

174
00:15:33,241 --> 00:15:35,411
You're so impatient.

175
00:15:35,491 --> 00:15:37,581
You should listen to what your elders say.

176
00:15:38,751 --> 00:15:40,541
Well, in other words,

177
00:15:40,621 --> 00:15:42,921
the world of man

178
00:15:43,001 --> 00:15:46,421
is getting older gradually, but surely.

179
00:15:46,501 --> 00:15:49,131
The Saxons destroyed the Romans,

180
00:15:49,211 --> 00:15:52,881
and we're going to destroy the Saxons next.

181
00:15:54,761 --> 00:15:58,311
The glory of the Roman Empire

182
00:15:58,391 --> 00:16:00,101
is a thing of the distant past.

183
00:16:03,561 --> 00:16:07,021
Anyways, according to what
the Christians are saying,

184
00:16:07,111 --> 00:16:12,071
the Last Judgment is coming
in only 20 years.

185
00:16:19,161 --> 00:16:22,911
On that day, God will kill everyone,

186
00:16:23,001 --> 00:16:25,921
and our world will be completely destroyed.

187
00:16:28,381 --> 00:16:29,501
Ragnarok.

188
00:16:35,221 --> 00:16:37,141
Look, Thorfinn.

189
00:16:37,221 --> 00:16:38,891
It's ironic, right?

190
00:16:41,061 --> 00:16:44,851
Dawn in the age of twilight.

191
00:17:02,161 --> 00:17:03,711
It's a horse.

192
00:17:05,831 --> 00:17:07,421
Is it an English soldier?

193
00:17:08,631 --> 00:17:11,711
No. He's an ally.

194
00:17:13,011 --> 00:17:17,681
That's weird.
I thought we were the only ones in this area.

195
00:17:17,761 --> 00:17:20,891
Hey! Wait!

196
00:17:21,931 --> 00:17:25,061
We're Askeladd's unit, under King Sweyn!

197
00:17:25,141 --> 00:17:27,191
Where did you come from?

198
00:17:28,861 --> 00:17:31,901
Oh, are you from the main army?

199
00:17:31,981 --> 00:17:34,651
I'm from Ragnar's unit
under His Highness Prince Canute!

200
00:17:34,741 --> 00:17:37,281
-I've got a message for the main force!
-Prince Canute?

201
00:17:37,361 --> 00:17:38,781
Are they close by?

202
00:17:41,491 --> 00:17:44,041
Unfortunately, the main army is far north.

203
00:17:44,121 --> 00:17:46,461
They're on their way home.

204
00:17:47,461 --> 00:17:50,501
Then what are you doing here?

205
00:17:50,591 --> 00:17:53,961
We're just trying to earn some pocket money
in that village over there.

206
00:17:54,051 --> 00:17:55,971
You separated from the army on your own?

207
00:17:56,051 --> 00:17:59,341
Well, don't be so stiff.

208
00:17:59,431 --> 00:18:01,551
Your horse looks tired.

209
00:18:01,641 --> 00:18:04,931
Do you want to trade it for a new one?

210
00:18:06,891 --> 00:18:07,981
Thorkell?

211
00:18:12,021 --> 00:18:14,571
Yes. He's almost there.

212
00:18:14,651 --> 00:18:18,951
There's 500 men. He took along only
his immediate followers.

213
00:18:19,031 --> 00:18:21,201
They're following the main army.

214
00:18:21,281 --> 00:18:23,541
They're going to reach Marlborough soon.

215
00:18:23,621 --> 00:18:25,201
Seriously?

216
00:18:25,291 --> 00:18:28,751
-They're so close!
-Attacking the main army with only 500?

217
00:18:28,831 --> 00:18:31,001
What about the unit laying siege to London?

218
00:18:31,081 --> 00:18:34,251
I thought Prince Canute had 4000 men.

219
00:18:34,341 --> 00:18:37,631
They were defeated a long time ago.

220
00:18:37,721 --> 00:18:40,391
I'm one of the survivors.

221
00:18:48,691 --> 00:18:49,601
What?

222
00:18:59,201 --> 00:19:01,111
With Thorkell leading them,

223
00:19:01,201 --> 00:19:03,161
they came out of the fortress.

224
00:19:21,181 --> 00:19:24,181
Take that!

225
00:19:25,721 --> 00:19:29,021
They were all as strong as bears.

226
00:19:30,311 --> 00:19:32,901
We couldn't do anything.

227
00:19:32,981 --> 00:19:35,361
They're making a beeline for the main army.

228
00:19:38,861 --> 00:19:41,031
Your Highness! Your Highness!

229
00:19:41,111 --> 00:19:44,701
Lord, may they rest in peace.

230
00:19:44,781 --> 00:19:47,291
-I pray that their souls may be saved--
-Your Highness!

231
00:19:47,371 --> 00:19:50,251
Thorkell is close!
We must leave at once!

232
00:20:01,221 --> 00:20:03,681
I found you, Prince!

233
00:20:11,601 --> 00:20:14,851
So, what happened to His Highness Canute?

234
00:20:14,941 --> 00:20:16,731
They captured him.

235
00:20:16,811 --> 00:20:19,231
He's with Thorkell's army.

236
00:20:19,321 --> 00:20:23,741
The remaining soldiers are trying to regroup
to go get His Highness back.

237
00:20:23,821 --> 00:20:26,531
But we have less than 400 men.

238
00:20:26,621 --> 00:20:28,911
And their morale is low.

239
00:20:28,991 --> 00:20:32,331
I'm on my way to ask the main army for help.

240
00:20:32,411 --> 00:20:36,081
Join us. We'd be grateful to have
even 100 extra men.

241
00:20:43,471 --> 00:20:46,591
What do you want to do? It's your decision.

242
00:20:46,681 --> 00:20:47,801
Askeladd.

243
00:20:54,811 --> 00:20:59,071
Come on. This isn't the time for us
to just fade into the twilight.

244
00:21:01,611 --> 00:21:02,441
What?

245
00:21:03,821 --> 00:21:05,361
Can't you hear it, Bjorn?

246
00:21:09,871 --> 00:21:12,121
The sound of the footsteps

247
00:21:12,201 --> 00:21:13,791
of Ragnarok.

248
00:21:36,101 --> 00:21:39,561
Bury him. And the horse he was riding.

249
00:21:39,651 --> 00:21:42,111
What? Okay.

250
00:21:43,651 --> 00:21:47,161
Listen up, guys!

251
00:21:47,241 --> 00:21:51,451
We're going to go save
His Highness Prince Canute!

252
00:21:51,531 --> 00:21:56,081
We're up against 500 of Thorkell's men!
But we're not going to ask for help!

253
00:21:56,161 --> 00:21:59,041
It's time to place our bets!

254
00:21:59,131 --> 00:22:01,841
His Highness Canute is second in line

255
00:22:01,921 --> 00:22:03,631
for the throne of Denmark.

256
00:22:03,711 --> 00:22:07,301
We're going to get a lot of money no matter
which side we hand him over to.

257
00:22:09,051 --> 00:22:11,431
Can you imagine...

258
00:22:12,471 --> 00:22:14,771
the rewards we'd be granted

259
00:22:14,851 --> 00:22:18,191
by the rulers of Denmark and England?

260
00:22:18,271 --> 00:22:21,811
We can't let someone else take it away from
right under our noses!

261
00:22:23,271 --> 00:22:24,901
Yeah!

262
00:22:24,981 --> 00:22:27,701
Let's do it! This is going to be ours!

263
00:22:27,781 --> 00:22:29,161
We'll do it!

264
00:22:38,661 --> 00:22:41,791
What are you going to do
now that you've stirred them up?

265
00:22:41,881 --> 00:22:45,251
We're up against Thorkell.
Do you have a plan for winning?

266
00:22:45,341 --> 00:22:46,171
Who knows.

267
00:22:47,301 --> 00:22:50,181
"Who knows"? Are you--

268
00:22:51,221 --> 00:22:53,261
This is the age of twilight, Bjorn.

269
00:22:54,851 --> 00:22:58,561
Let's go out with a bang.
